      "side": 1,
      "message": "The spurious wakeup should not result in the command being sent again.\nThe same applies to interleaved events like [Index Added].\n\nI don\u0027t think that you need to send the command more than once anyway, as new interfaces will be notified with the [Index Added] event.\n\nThe proper structure should be:\n\n1. Send [Read Index List] command\n2. 1st loop wait for [Read Index List Complete] response. All [Index Added] events received in the same loop can be ignored (the same interfaces will be reported in the response).\n3. If no interface is found; enter a poll loop to wait for [Index Added] events for a fixed timeout duration.\n\nThe current implementation does 1. and 2., but fails if no interface is found.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 146,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 148,
        "endChar": 5
      },
